# DECIMAL arithmetic, SUM and AVG (ADR 0021 rules 4 to 7, 12, 13 and 18; docs/sql-subset.md). + - * take DuckDB's
# types: an integer counts as DECIMAL(5,0), (10,0), (19,0) or (38,0), widths beyond 18 digits from two operands of at
# most 18 are capped to 18, beyond 38 to 38, and a value past the capped width is an error with DuckDB's message. SUM is
# an exact DECIMAL(38,s), AVG a DOUBLE as DuckDB computes it. Rows 0 to 13 of decimals hold the columns' extremes, so
# the value records read rows 14 and up.

query IDDDDDDDD nosort
SELECT id, p + q, p - d9_2, p * q, d9_2 * d9_2, p + id, id * p, -p, -d38_10 FROM decimals WHERE id >= 14 ORDER BY id
